  "title": "The First Noel",
  "composer": "Traditional",
  "about": "The First Noel is an English carol, and nobody knows who wrote its tune. It is thought to come from Cornwall, in the far south-west of England. Davies Gilbert printed it in 1823, and William Sandys printed it in 1833. John Stainer set it for choirs in 1871, and his version is the one sung today.",
  "funFact": "Noel comes from the French word Noël, and that comes from the Latin word for birth.",
